{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact sales-design draft3 1469f2f18a883fe8972cdadb32fcbcf85e7ac623, sole primary82e303e8, notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md. Primary read first in full (475 lines); old777/c02 review was replaced before verdict. The prospect/bid/calendar package shapes and the distinction between an expert's supply and the team's review are useful. Buyer exclusion in the first bid version, whole-room visibility, absent private custody and deferred integrations are stated honestly. Five corrections remain before approval.\n\nF1 high — Use grant forms the declared runtime actually has (4.1 and4.3, lines182–199,294–297). ActType.grant is one fixed action string; declared guards do not dynamically choose a grant from requirement.domain or express review-answer as bid.technical OR bid.own. The native judge checks that exact action before evaluating the item's guards (contract/src/definition.ts:92–106; derive/src/judge.ts:327–344). Choose explicit per-domain supply acts and per-kind approval acts, or another concrete existing-form mapping; a common explicit review action may be granted to owner and sales engineer. Add the native domain and assigned-expert/reviewer signer checks needed for the claimed ownership. A view's routing or hidden button supplies no authority. Also resolve the interaction's statement that the agent signs ask-expert: its table grants bid.draft only draft-answer/flag, and the text says agents hold neither domain nor review grant. Either make asking a permitted separate agent action or leave it to the named people. This is a small authority mapping, not a new native dynamic-grant feature.\n\nF2 high — Make submission completeness and approvals non-vacuous and tied to the same current assembly (4.2/4.3 and C3). Draft3 corrected the old 'none assigned/drafted' guard to every requirement reviewed/declined; keep that correction. However 'every approval granted' still permits no approval items, or only an old granted approval while the price/terms have changed. State which approvals are required, require their presence and current price/terms references, and make submit use the exact sealed rendering/answer/approval set. Import/mapping completeness must cover the source rows intended for that response; absent or unresolved mappings cannot disappear from the set whose completeness is checked. C3 imports40rows but supplies/reviews only6 before assembling: explicitly review or decline the remaining34 with reasons, or first demonstrate incomplete assembly refusal before finishing. No missing approval, unaccounted source row or edited answer may become an apparently complete submission.\n\nF3 high — Separate sending from confirmed publication (4.2/4.3,5.2/5.3). The note goes from submit/publish sending publish-file to the exact bytes having gone out, a publication receipt on the item and a published log, but provides no pending/unknown/refused/superseded outcome boundary. Receiving/applied delivery of publish-file does not prove the later Git push succeeded. The landed Destination retains queued/reserved/unresolved/terminal publication states; unknown holds the slot and is not blindly resent. Its receipt binds the full sending scope/incarnation, source fact and send ordinal, path and content digest (platform/README.md; platform/src/destination.ts:2581ff,2621ff,2672ff; scope/test/application-publication.test.ts unknown/restart and superseded cases). Keep bid sealing and post approval as local decisions; retain a pending or unknown publication until the matching confirmed receipt/readback establishes the exact approved bytes, with explicit refusal/supersession behavior. State the supported confirmation path rather than assuming a send result is that receipt. Revisions must not transfer an earlier receipt to newer content. Manual channel postings remain attributed member reports.\n\nF4 medium — Define retirement within today's file-write operation or defer actual deletion (5.2, lines385–386). publish-file accepts path and text content, and its tree builder inserts/replaces bytes; it has no delete field or remove-path variant (platform/src/destination.ts:2581–2585; platform/src/destination-objects.ts TreeFile/editTree). Empty content produces a file, not deletion. Choose a documented tombstone/replacement or bounded index rewrite under the existing write operation, keeping its publication outcome separate, or defer repository-file deletion. 'Publishes its removal the same way' presently assumes an operation today's forms do not provide.\n\nF5 medium — Bound the intake before claiming the few-hundred-row single bid queue (4.2/4.4/C3). Current complete many-source projections and native item-query pages have a100-row maximum, and a routed carousel evaluates for only after obtaining the complete source. An incomplete page refuses; routing by domain/member does not make a200-row source complete. Result/text/field budgets also remain finite (bytes/src/application-projection-types.ts:9–11; contract/src/item-query.ts:7; bytes/src/application-projection-read.ts completeness check). Document the first version's finite row and text/payload limits, including refusal of oversized input before a misleading partial import, or an explicit bounded partition/sharding plan. Deferring larger matrices is sufficient; no paging or higher admission limit is required by this review. The40-row C3 example fits the row count but does not establish the current 'few hundred' claim.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: the existing open/transition items, fixed grant actions, signer/field guards, timed rules, declared cards/records/logs and routed complete carousels can support bounded versions of the three processes. Multiple native owned scopes and Git file publication are real landed mechanisms; hosted agent teams remain a design as the note says. The several-scope implementation is completed through M2b's ownership/birth work as well as M2a's interface, so link the M2b implementation when identifying that shipped capability. The linked roadmap's older 'no declared several-scope application yet' paragraph is historical/stale; actual landed source/implementation witnesses support the mechanism. Do not infer these sales definitions or hosted instances are implemented.\n\nSecurity conclusion: scope membership, exact native action grants and signer guards must enforce domain/owner decisions independently of routing. An agent draft, expert supply, team review, local seal and outside publication each retain their own authority and evidence. Buyer-outside-first-version and links/digests without custody are appropriate boundaries; neither a source link nor a signed import is independently retained source-file custody.\n\nSimplification conclusion: keep each package small, choose explicit static action names and a bounded first version, and reuse current Destination writes. The five changes can be made in this design note without a generic integration system, new grant interpreter, new native deletion API or expanded query limits. Preserve the current deferral after plan033; this review commissions no implementation.\n\nValidation: entire draft3 and prior drafts read, all10 local links/heading fragments resolve, whitespace clean. Only this new Markdown path changes from Main2127d5c5; draft1 tree comparison preserved all2291 base leaves and later revisions remain confined to the same path. Draft3 SHA256e18e4bc64593e6dca35a161c5392e641678768c6d9362ae9ec8ba0fdb5e16437. Read actual landed contract/judge/projection/publication code and existing native publication tests; did not run those suites or invent a runtime acceptance result. Native prepare binds7f569087 /28988cd9 /report82e303e8 at this exact head. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-sales-design-jne3y8sq retains primary copies and validation. Documentation only: no gate, source/test edits, package installs, provider/publication/deployment action.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572